/**
 * /gym-safety-accessories — "Gym Safety Accessories & Protection Barriers"
 * conversion + SEO / AEO / GEO hub for the Zain Curb Stone range.
 *
 * Bespoke page (not the YAML-driven generic HubPage). Structure, helper classes
 * and motion mirror src/pages/gym-flooring-rolls.astro, src/pages/rubber-gym-tiles.astro
 * and src/pages/gym-fitness-flooring.astro so every gym hub reads as one system.
 *
 * ─── ROUTING ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 * This file produces the route /gym-safety-accessories. It does NOT collide
 * with src/pages/[...slug].astro: the only content entry whose `path` begins
 * with /gym-safety-accessories is the product spoke
 * (src/content/products/curb-stone.yaml → /gym-safety-accessories/curb-stone).
 * No hub YAML owns the bare /gym-safety-accessories path, so getStaticPaths
 * needs no change — this page becomes the visible parent index for that spoke
 * (same setup as rubber-gym-tiles.astro and gym-flooring-rolls.astro).
 *
 * ─── ICON / IMAGE IMPLEMENTATION (deviates from the build request) ───────
 *   - Icons: the request named `lucide-react`. React is not part of this
 *     Astro stack (zero-JS by default, no @astrojs/react). To keep the page
 *     zero-JS and match every sibling hub, the SAME Lucide glyphs are inlined
 *     as 24×24 stroke path data in the `icon` map below — identical output,
 *     no runtime.
 *   - Images: the request named Astro's <Image /> (astro:assets). Every asset
 *     for this page lives in /public (not /src), and <Image /> only optimises
 *     src-imported assets. All sibling hubs use plain <img> from /images with
 *     explicit width/height + loading/decoding, so this page does the same for
 *     consistency. Sources were converted from the supplied JPEGs to optimised
 *     WebP (~4.0 MB → 0.5 MB, ~88% smaller; JPEG sources deleted, matching the
 *     sibling hubs).
 *
 * ─── DATA INTEGRITY FLAGS (CLAUDE.md §0 "Data Integrity" + §6) ────────────
 *   - The §5 technical table is DESCRIPTIVE only (composition, behaviour,
 *     climate, install method) — no numbers are asserted. curb-stone.yaml still
 *     lists Dimensions (L×W×H), Weight and Colour options as unfilled TODOs;
 *     collect and publish those before go-live.
 *   - Hero primary CTA points at /contact (the real contact route). The build
 *     request asked for /contact-us/, which does not exist in this project —
 *     same decision as the sibling hubs.
 *   - No purpose-built 1200×630 OG image for this page (falls back to the hero).
 *
 * businessSchema is intentionally NOT set (CLAUDE.md §5 puts LocalBusiness on
 * the homepage and contact page only). Breadcrumbs.astro emits BreadcrumbList;
 * FAQPage + Product JSON-LD are inline, matching the sibling hub pages.
 */
